+// Decoding the held Opus into deck-ready frames is the last step before a fade,
+// and while it runs the cue can do nothing but wait. Upstream asks for it
+// DECODE_LEAD_SECONDS before the fade would start, which is generous in a browser
+// tab and not here, where separating the track after next is spending the same
+// seconds: a decode that overruns costs the entire transition, silently, one second
+// from the end. Nothing about the request has to wait for the clock — the Opus is
+// held the moment the stems are staged — so it goes out then, and the only price is
+// holding the decoded frames for the rest of the track instead of the last few
+// seconds of it.
+function requestStagedDecode(): void {
+  const videoId = staging.beginStemsDecode();
+  if (videoId === null) return;
+  postToWindow({ type: "blk-request-staged-deck", videoId });
+}
